{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641941,"nonce":"bBvmXI34jkx/Nd0MyDAISgAN0Lg=","title":"Fibers allocate a fresh mmap stack each; no stack cache","message":"krio_adapter/src/fiber.rs fiber_new: every fiber (Python generator, Lua coroutine, async task) gets an mmap plus an mprotect guard page and a munmap when freed. Lua requests 64 MiB per coroutine (zyntax_lua/src/library/coroutines.rs). Creation also inserts into several SipHash thread-local maps and fiber_free scans every task's set.\n\nRepro: 100,000 coroutine.wrap(function(n) coroutine.yield(n) end) run to completion: 2.2 s in zylua, 16 ms LuaJIT, 38 ms Lua 5.5. 100,000 Python generators with two yields: about 350 ms, CPython 12 ms. Suspended coroutines keep their mappings and are scanned by every collection (stack_windows): a 400k-yield loop after the creation loop slowed from 0.5 s to 3.3 s. On Linux each stack is two VMAs, so about 32k live coroutines may reach vm.max_map_count and trip the mmap failed assert (not tested on Linux).\n\nDirection: free list of stacks, modest default size, avoid per-fiber SipHash maps.","files":null}]}